# Copy this file to `.env.development.local` (gitignored, never commit real
# values) so `npm run dev` resolves the LOCAL Supabase stack, not whatever
# `.env.local` on this machine happens to contain — `.env.local` has held a
# production Supabase URL before (see
# docs/INCIDENT_2026-07-10_PRODUCTION_SIDE_EFFECT.md). Vite's own env
# precedence for `npm run dev` (mode "development") is:
#   process.env > .env.development.local > .env.local > .env.development > .env
# so this file, once created, always wins over .env.local for local dev.
#
# The predev guard (scripts/dev/assertLocalDevTarget.mjs) checks this
# resolution before Vite starts and blocks anything that isn't
# 127.0.0.1/localhost — this file is what makes that check pass.
#
# Values below are Supabase CLI's well-known LOCAL-ONLY demo credentials —
# identical on every machine running `npx supabase start`, not a secret.
# Get the current values for your machine with: npx supabase status
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0
